Noting that your project mentions population-based and evolutionary approaches, this inevitably leads me to reflect on the definition of life.
From a biological perspective, life is the comprehensive manifestation of a series of complex phenomena exhibited by organisms.
However, for self-evolving intelligent agents, this is not an ideal description, as these agents lack the structural and characteristic features of traditional organisms.
Therefore, having intelligent agents mimic biological traits does not truly endow them with life.
I believe life hinges on two core traits: first, the capacity to maintain its own state—survival and inertia. Second, the propensity for continuous expansion—growth and reproduction.
